From 349300e11f0736dca8a931a9a5bae77868b92d15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lenOS hardening <hardening@lenos.invalid>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:26:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] asteroids: disable 2G (GSM) in default network mode to block
 IMSI-catcher downgrade

ro.telephony.default_network 26 -> 28: drops GSM (2G) while keeping
NR (5G) + LTE (4G) + WCDMA (3G).

26 = NETWORK_MODE_NR_LTE_GSM_WCDMA (2G-capable)
28 = NETWORK_MODE_NR_LTE_WCDMA (no GSM)

Rationale: GSM has no network-to-phone authentication, so a fake base
station (IMSI catcher / Stingray) can force a downgrade and intercept
calls/SMS and track the IMSI. Removing GSM from the default mode removes
the downgrade target.

Tradeoff: no service in 2G-only coverage areas (some regions keep 2G
alive until ~2030); emergency calls there may be affected.

Verified against lineage-23.2 RILConstants.java:
  NETWORK_MODE_NR_LTE_GSM_WCDMA = 26, NETWORK_MODE_NR_LTE_WCDMA = 28.
---
 system_ext.prop | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/system_ext.prop b/system_ext.prop
index b96d772..8dba3e9 100644
--- a/system_ext.prop
+++ b/system_ext.prop
@@ -44,5 +44,8 @@ ro.vendor.qti.va_aosp.support=1
 
 # Telephony
 ril.subscription.types=NV,RUIM
-ro.telephony.default_network=26,26
+# lenOS: drop GSM (2G) from the default network mode to prevent IMSI-catcher
+# downgrade attacks. 26 = NR+LTE+GSM+WCDMA (2G-capable); 28 = NR+LTE+WCDMA (no GSM).
+# Tradeoff: no service in 2G-only areas; emergency calls there may be affected.
+ro.telephony.default_network=28,28
 telephony.lteOnCdmaDevice=1
-- 
